WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.980
Pirari Academy

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.980
Final Exam

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.980
Announcement

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.820
<i>Hello there, my lovely 
maidens from class S!</i>

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.050
<i>It's everyone's favorite 
student council president!</i>

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:13.280
<i>Did I surprise you?</i>

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.430
<i>Exams are so boring I thought 
the least I could do</i>

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.200
<i>was make it more fun and 
get everyone fired up!</i>

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.970
<i>Final exams happen twice a year, 
in both summer and winter.</i>

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.230
<i>And in class S alone,</i>

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.090
<i>there's a practical exam to test 
students' Logicalist aptitude.</i>

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.660
<i>The results from this exam
will impact your career options in the future.</i>

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.520
<i>So listen carefully and do your 
best to prepare for the exam.</i>

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.220
<i>Now then, here's your principal.</i>

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.220
Please wait a moment.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:40.980
Wasn't that girl…

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.140
The girl we saw in town?

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.570
<i>This year, for our first-year
class S practical exam,</i>

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:51.690
<i>we have specially invited
active-duty Logicalists as examiners.</i>

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:53.740
<i>Chloe Maxwell.</i>

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:55.730
<i>Mana Asuha.</i>

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.450
<i>Yukari Nanahoshi.</i>

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.090
<i>During your practical exam, you 
will learn from their teamwork,</i>

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.880
<i>and your collective skills as 
Logicalists will be tested.</i>

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:06.390
<i>Details will be released on the day of—</i>

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:07.460
<i>Vice-Principal!</i>

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.320
<i>You're forgetting a very important message.</i>

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.700
<i>Wh-What do you mean?</i>

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.720
<i>They should be sure to wear their school 
swimsuit under their gym uniform!</i>

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>I repeat—</i>

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:21.970
Episode 5

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:21.970
A Journey of a Thousand Miles
 Begins With Effort

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:56.780
Miss Fujisaki!

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.500
Let me say this before you ask any questions:

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.030
Everything you just heard is true.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.460
Details of the exam will be 
revealed on the day of the test.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.750
So even that swimsuit part was true.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.220
Miss Fujisaki!

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.660
If what's on the exam is a secret, 
what are we supposed to do to prepare?

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.820
In your case, you should first look at your

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.730
Japanese, mathematics, 
sociology, science and…

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.440
I'm sorry. You were asking about 
the practical exam, right?

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.990
If you want to be a strong Logicalist,

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.160
you have to train in every area.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.060
Every area?

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.560
If you only focus on your 
physical strengths and skills

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.850
you'll one day find yourself off-balance.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.190
Be sure to train both your 
heart and mind as well.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.190
S-Sure?

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.120
I went out of my way to be sure I finished 
preparing for my written exams early.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.060
But if I don't know anything 
about the practical exam,

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.220
no amount of time will help 
me make a good plan for it.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.840
That's true.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.130
Nina-san.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:59.050
Do you know what kind of people the 
Logicalists that will be our examiners are?

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.630
Yes. They're highly capable.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.210
I knew it.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.870
Do you really think we'll 
be able to defeat them?

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:08.540
They said the exam was about 
our collective skills,

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.050
so I don't think it'll just be a mock battle.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:11.640
Well then.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.610
At the very least, I shall have 
to train more

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.400
to up my grasp on the basics any way I can.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.300
You'll be fine.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.910
No matter the subject, 
no matter the opponent,

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.070
you'll always come out on top!

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.930
Because we'll support you.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.950
Yup, yup. No way anyone can top us 3 on 1!

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.860
Karin, Karen.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.550
I'm happy to hear you say that,

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:34.640
but exams exist to test 
an individual's strengths.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:35.680
Aww.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:36.660
But if we're just a bit sneaky…

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:37.460
You mustn't.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.100
Do your best, fair and square.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.050
Understood.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.050
Got it!

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.390
It's our first practical exam as first-years!

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:49.600
And the student who will claim
first place will be me, Yayoi Tachibana!

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.310
Practical Exam

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.310
in

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.310
days

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:59.110
Now, let's get started with our training!

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.070
Practical exam in 4 days

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.660
Practical exam in 3 days

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.070
Practical exam in 2 days

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.790
Practical exam

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.790
in

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.790
Days

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.790
Written exam day

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.440
Mistress.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.960
Can't eat more...

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.070
It seems they really gave it their all.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.340
Mistress.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:37.660
Do your best.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:45.370
I swear I will definitely take first place,

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:48.950
so that I can be worthy of being your mistress.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.480
A very good morning to you, Nina-san.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.800
Morning.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.470
I mustn't allow myself to lose.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.220
You're running quite fast, aren't you?

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:15.220
It's just luck.

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:16.930
Is that right?

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:21.090
Nina-san, lately… you've been…

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:24.500
having mock battles every 
day… after school.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.400
You too, right?

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.970
Well, I just want to do everything that I can.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.640
You're right.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.260
Today's the written exams,

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:52.140
so I only wanted to work up a light sweat.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:56.930
We ended in a tie today, but 
I'll win next time for sure!

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.390
You really hate losing, don't you?

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:02.040
I won't deny that.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:06.230
I realize as a Logicalist, I'm 
just an egg that's yet to hatch.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.400
But I still intend to win against 
you during the practical exam.

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:16.090
I may have been on active duty,

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:18.440
but when it comes to natural aptitude…

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:21.500
I'm not much different from 
the other students in class S.

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:25.000
But you intend to take first 
place, do you not, Nina-san?

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:27.830
I do.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:31.360
But when it comes to the practical exam,

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:33.880
I consider a number of 
students tough opponents.

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:35.700
Like Lion-san?

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:44.230
Of course, and you too.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.190
All right, everyone's here, right?

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:59.230
No missing students, right?

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:00.500
Here!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.210
Okay, I'll start my explanation 
on the practical exam.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:08.250
In the simplest terms, this 
exam is an obstacle race.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.760
<b>Practical exam</b>

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.760
<b>detailed explanation</b>

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.760
There are three checkpoints.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.760
The academy entrance bridge.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.260
The sheer cliff.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.760
And the connecting passageway.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:19.770
Get through all these obstacles and reach 
the goal at the principal's office.

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:22.100
And most importantly…

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:24.790
these are survivors in need of aid.

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:25.840
Stuffed toys!

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:26.960
Cute!

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:31.330
It will be your mission to safely deliver 
these stuffed friends to the goal.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.930
All right, you're Yan-Yan.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:36.070
If they should be injured or you are 
incapacitated, you will be disqualified.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.620
You'll be Lawrie!

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.070
I name you Kero-beros.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:39.370
You're not allowed to hurt other students,

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:38.730
Let's get along.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.840
Tuna! Tuna!

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:43.080
but other than that, you're all free 
to use your powers however you like.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:47.330
Finally, you will only be allowed to Trance 
twice during the entirety of the exam.

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:51.680
Additionally, each Trance may 
only last up to three minutes.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:54.430
As we don't know what obstacles lie ahead,

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.260
it would be foolish to Trance 
without a second thought.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.690
The exam will be scored out 
of a total of 10 points.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:01.030
Points will be awarded for speed,

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:04.270
but also for how you conduct 
yourself as a Logicalist.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:06.780
Now, are you all ready?

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:07.780
Yes!

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:10.270
Ready!

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:12.310
Bang!

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:22.170
It's Miss Kagura.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:23.110
And she's…

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:24.080
What do we do?

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.780
Don't ask me.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:27.400
There's no way.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.290
Nope.

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:29.620
Yay!

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:30.540
What?!

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:31.740
So that's it!

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:33.210
Us too!

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:34.800
Off they go!

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.090
Strip!

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.630
Fishies, fishies!

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:40.850
Pardon me!

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.670
The early bird gets the worm.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:43.970
That's the strategy I'm going with.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:48.600
Guess I should have expected 
no one would fight me.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.610
I'll just have to get in 
their way then instead.

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:00.530
We'll get to the goal first 
at this rate, Kero-beros.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.990
Woah, look at Karin-chan.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.250
She's already that high up.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.210
They're faster than I expected.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.740
Kero-beros!

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:32.360
<i>Farewell.</i>

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:34.690
One out.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:39.150
What is this? Gross!

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:42.280
Just a little bit more.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.660
This is quite the problem.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.710
Time to initiate operations!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.510
How do you like them apples?!

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:03.760
Wait up! I'm coming too!

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:05.250
Trance!

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.150
Mana-senpai!

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.400
How about we move to the next point?

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:29.510
I made it!

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:32.790
I won't be taking first at this rate.

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:37.800
<i>Oh dear. No!</i>

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.520
Yayoi-chan.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.020
Lion-san.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:57.480
I'm happy to see my
vines got to you in time.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:03.150
It would have been dangerous if you 
fell from all the way up there.

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:05.160
Why did you save me?

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.050
Huh?

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:09.880
When I thought you were in danger, 
I just moved without thinking.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:12.860
What's the matter?

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:14.920
I must retire from this race.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:16.420
Huh? Why?

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:19.400
Because it is against the rules…

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:21.280
to borrow the strength of another.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:22.300
Why?

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:23.300
Why?

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:28.660
Isn't our exam to take our 
stuffed friends to the goal?

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:34.140
It will be your mission to safely deliver 
these stuffed friends to the goal.

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:37.360
You're all free to use your 
powers however you like.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.360
I…

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:43.360
may have had my judgment clouded 
by a grave misunderstanding.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:45.420
Is this okay?

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:46.600
It's fine.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:47.990
Their actions fall within the given rules.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:52.250
The only ones left are…

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.910
Looks like Mahiro-san and 
Karen-san have dropped out.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:57.250
Next, we have Nina-san.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:01.250
Let us make our sound
in the gaps between the waves.

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:04.720
You're as good as ever.

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:06.090
You too, Chloe-san.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.290
Logic Drive!

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:14.220
Last Final Finish Sword!

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.560
Try that trick all you want,
it won't work!

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:32.080
She almost got me that time.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:33.790
I can still—

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.540
Was that meant to be a warning shot?

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:38.420
I wonder?

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.880
There's no reason for you to hold back.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.630
Logic Drive!

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:44.400
Crap!

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:44.900
Yukari.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:46.010
G-Got it!

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:54.730
I did it?

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:07.490
I wish I could do something 
for you since you beat me.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:09.360
No. A disqualification is a disqualification.

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:11.370
Now then!

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.410
It's my turn.

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:17.540
Gate access! Disfia!

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:21.320
It's our turn! Qipao!

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:25.370
<i>They look tough.</i>

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.420
<i>Let's see how far we can get.</i>

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.160
<i>My name is Yayoi Tachibana!</i>

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:59.410
<i>The woman who will one day 
stand as the top Logicalist!</i>

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:02.380
I like it!

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:04.720
My name's Chloe Maxwell.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:05.840
Come at me!

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:07.410
Mana Mana, Yukarin.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:08.610
I don't want you butting in.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:10.550
Absolutely not?

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.880
Absolutely not!

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:12.470
I see.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:14.850
Now, let's go!

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.000
Isn't this…?

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:47.990
You're not going to catch me from behind!

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:49.670
No way!

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:51.170
Logic Drive!

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:55.060
Last Final Finish Sword!

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:04.020
I'll have you know that I'm 
the mistress of two ninjas.

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:09.780
Wha?!

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:11.510
Are you serious?!

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:12.810
Yayoi-chan!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:17.160
When did that happen?

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:18.920
The very beginning.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.890
You see, when you were starting your fight,

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:24.670
she was already on the move
under the bridge.

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:26.670
Absolutely not?

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:27.980
Absolutely not!

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:28.630
I see.

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:31.130
Why didn't you tell me?

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:34.630
Well, you told us not to butt in.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.140
It's tuna!

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:41.100
Here's Yan-Yan.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.440
Bienvenue.

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:46.900
Busy grading.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:51.400
<b>1st: Liones Yelistratova
2nd: Yayoi Tachibana
3rd: Nina Alexandrovna
4th: Mahiro Kyobashi
Karen Kiritani
Karin Kiritani</b>

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:51.400
I got… first?

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.260
Yay!

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:54.830
Congrats!

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:56.410
You sure gave it your all.

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:58.120
You get a gold star.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.450
That tickles!

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:10.000
Why did you let Lion go first?

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:13.760
Our goal was to deliver the survivors safely.

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:17.060
Lion-san was the one who figured that out.

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:22.630
Yayoi, you may have what it takes 
to be a commanding officer.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:29.680
Yes, but of course.

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:32.440
I'm the future chief of ALCA after all!

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:39.120
The water here feels great.

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:42.450
All my fatigue has just blown away.

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:45.960
But I wanted to try fighting you, too.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:47.430
Me?

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:49.190
You had some good moves out there.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.900
You're good at fighting, aren't you?

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.090
I dunno?

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:54.210
When you consider Rosa-san's abilities,

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:56.280
you're well suited to support too, right?

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.840
Yeah. And that was a good 
plan you came up with.

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:00.590
Thanks!

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:04.260
But Yayoi-chan was the one 
who came up with the plan.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:09.570
Yayoi-chan's really smart 
and reliable. She's amazing!

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:12.400
And on top of that, she 
wakes me up in the morning,

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:13.840
and she's the class representative...

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:15.320
Um…

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:18.030
And she has panda panties!

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:20.860
I believe your final point had 
nothing to do with anything!

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:28.410
So the only reason I got first 
was because of Yayoi-chan!

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:34.160
Lion-san, you had better come 
to realize your own strengths.

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:38.420
Gosh! You should know that I see you 
as a rival that I will one day defeat!

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:39.930
Aww.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.680
I-Is something about that 
not to your liking?!

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:44.460
I'd rather be friends.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.810
You're my friend and my rival.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:51.050
Then I'm happy.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.860
<b>Pirari Academy
School Festival</b>

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.860
<b>October 21st-22nd</b>

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:00.860
A school festival?

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:03.520
It's to open the school 
to the general public

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:08.030
so they can expand their understanding 
of Logicalists and Foreigners, huh?

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:10.120
I see!

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:12.340
Lion.

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:26.930
What's this for?

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:30.150
Close your eyes while holding that 
mirror in your hands like that.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:35.360
How do you feel when you Trance with Rosa?

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.940
Like I'm calling out to her.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.280
Imagine that feeling.

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:45.950
Just as I thought.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:47.910
You can open your eyes.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:52.080
Huh? It's all green.

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:55.960
This mirror shows its users 
their heart's inner balance.

00:19:57.450 --> 00:20:00.690
A Trance is a state of being in 
which a Logicalist and Foreigner

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:05.720
each share half of their Logic 
with one another and become one.

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:10.960
In your case, you empathize strongly 
with the Foreigner's feelings,

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.970
and as such have a tendency to give too 
much of your Logic to your partner.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:17.360
Green shows Monolium.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:21.220
In other words, you're entrusting yourself 
to Rosa so much that you show that.

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:22.740
I am?

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:27.160
Lion, I want you to realize that 
you're in a very dangerous position.

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:30.210
If you can't learn to retain your own will,

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:35.250
it's very possible that you could damage 
both yourself and your surroundings.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:02.150
Nina-chan!

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:04.180
Lion-san?

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.110
What brings you here?

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:08.600
Um… Well…

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:13.370
Who knows?

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:16.450
I'm going back to the dorm now. You?

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:18.600
Yup! Let's go home together.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:22.510
I wonder what's for dinner?

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.050
I hope it's tuna.

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:02.130
I knew it. I knew how it'd go.

00:23:02.130 --> 00:23:05.120
I knew the group date couldn't 
wouldn't turn out well.

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:07.130
But you know? You know?

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:09.610
Yeah, it really went south.

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:11.730
Oh, you mean that mixer you were setting up?

00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:13.650
It was the worst!

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:15.790
They were all so built, but all so weak!

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:16.550
What?

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:25.800
Next Episode

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:20.830
Exactly. Honestly, I can't 
stand a guy that's weaker than me.

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:25.270
I mean, a normal human could 
never be stronger than us. Right?

00:23:25.270 --> 00:23:28.300
That's why what's most important 
is how smart they are.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:31.090
Now's the era of hot guys! 
That's all there is to it.

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:34.600
Also, even better if he's 
tall and makes good money!

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:36.060
You've sure got high hopes.

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:40.560
Man, I wish I could find 
someone like you, Senpai.
